{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793310000000-engineer-frame-nan.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-16 02:05:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-16 09:05 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: frame.cljc free-env comparison must be NaN-reflexive on JS and Dart (post-phase-8 follow-up; uncommitted)\nRole: VM Runtime\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-10-16 09:05 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: codex implements; Fable reviews; independent of the srvm-phase8 merge decision\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8frame (branch srvm-frame-nan @ srvm-phase8 6dceede9). Read ./collab/1792057828000-architect-8f3-nan-ruling.report.md section 5 \"Known gap\" and its F1 tuple= / cbor/content= rationale. The site: src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/frame.cljc ~:139-143 `(= (apply dissoc bindings names) (apply dissoc (:free-env task) names))` compares two binding MAPS with host `=`; a NaN-valued free binding in a captured, parked or waiting frame is refused as :free-env-mismatch on JS and Dart (the JVM passes by shared-box identity). Fix: compare the remaining bindings slotwise (same key set, then per key) using the encoder's own equality `dao.jing.cbor/content=` where values are plain data, guarded the way yin.vm.data/data-content= (src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc ~:466) guards callables, refs and cursor cells (read it; reuse it if it is the right predicate and public; otherwise add one small private helper beside the site, no new namespace). Find any OTHER host-= comparison of runtime VALUES (not ids/pcs/kinds) on the carrier/frame/custody validation path of src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/frame.cljc and src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows*.cljc and fix the same way ONLY if it is the same bug; list the rest as not-same-bug. Tests (portable .cljc, in test/yin/vm/semantic/frame_test.cljc): a frame/task whose free-env carries a NaN binding (a fresh box via (* 1.0 ##NaN) vs a literal ##NaN) validates (no :free-env-mismatch) and a real mismatch (NaN vs 1.0, and a differing key) is still refused :free-env-mismatch; also 0.0 vs -0.0 stays a mismatch if cbor/content= says so. Prove the test would fail without the fix where the JVM allows (mutate to host =, note JVM may not fail because of shared boxes: say so honestly; the Node/Dart lanes are the proof, the orchestrator runs them). Same prohibitions: no docs/design edits (update docs/agents/known-gaps.md: close the frame.cljc:141 row with this commit's evidence), no test/yang, no src/yang, no commit/stage. Foreground: kondo on changed files; `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.semantic.frame-test -n yin.vm.semantic.vm-test -n yin.vm.semantic.effects-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`; whole JVM quick tier `clojure -M:test -e :slow` (loopback/antlr: request unrestricted). Report ./collab/<ms>-engineer-frame-nan.report.md with Completed-GMT/Completed-Local/Coding-Agent/Session-ID, exact diff summary, counts, mutant result, truthful. End READY or BLOCKED.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
